{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"definechart","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineChart"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\nimport { portal } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip/portal'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineChart"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts a complete chart spec, a responsive configuration, or an\nexisting definition plus replacement behavior:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function defineChart<const TMarks, const TSpec>(\n  spec: TSpec,\n): StaticChartDefinition<InferredDatum, InferredX, InferredY>\n\nfunction defineChart<const TSpec>(\n  chart: (context: ChartBuildContext) => TSpec,\n): ResponsiveChartDefinition<InferredDatum, InferredX, InferredY>\n\nfunction defineChart<const TSpec>(\n  config: ResponsiveChartConfig<TSpec>,\n): ResponsiveChartDefinition<InferredDatum, InferredX, InferredY>\n\nfunction defineChart<TDefinition, TOptions>(\n  definition: TDefinition,\n  options: TOptions,\n): Omit<TDefinition, keyof TOptions> & TOptions","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"static-definitions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static definitions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a static definition when its data and visual options are already known:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { scaleUtc } from 'd3-scale'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks: [lineY(rows, { x: 'date', y: 'value' })],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: scaleUtc },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear, nice: true, grid: true },\n  },\n\n  focus: 'group-x',\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    portal,\n    anchor: 'group-center',\n    placement: ['top', 'right', 'left', 'bottom'],\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"responsive-definitions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responsive definitions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a configuration object when the spec depends on the resolved chart\nsurface:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  svgAnimation: true,\n  chart: ({ width }) => ({\n    marks: [barY(rows, { x: 'category', y: 'value' })],\n    scales: {\n      x: { scale: scaleBand },\n      y: {\n        scale: scaleLinear,\n        nice: true,\n        axis: { ticks: { count: width < 480 ? 4 : 7 } },\n        grid: true,\n      },\n    },\n  }),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The builder receives:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current full surface width"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current full surface height"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultTheme"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTheme"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Platform defaults before the returned spec applies its theme"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"height"},{"type":"text","value":" are controlled by the host. The builder can read them but\ndoes not return or own them."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"definition-behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definition behavior"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartDefinitionOptions<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>"},{"type":"text","value":" contains "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focus"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusRing"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"selection"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"controls"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cursor"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxFocusDistance"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"spatialIndex"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"svgAnimation"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pointer"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keyboard"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tooltip"},{"type":"text","value":". These options\nbelong to both static and responsive definitions. Hosts and framework adapters\ndo not override them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"focusRing"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":", or a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartFocusRingOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" object with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"radius"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strokeWidth"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fill"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stroke"},{"type":"text","value":". Omitted fields keep the built-in\ndefaults, including the focused point's resolved color for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stroke"},{"type":"text","value":". The same\nvalue on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"theme.focusRing"},{"type":"text","value":" provides a default, while an explicitly supplied\ndefinition-level value takes precedence. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./focus-and-interaction.md#built-in-focus-ring","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus and interaction"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartControl"},{"type":"text","value":" resolves after final scales and plot bounds exist. It can\nprovide renderer-neutral fallback nodes and an optional host control. Control\nIDs and host-control identities must be unique. Browser hosts remove a\ncontrol's fallback before painting and own its update, renderer replacement,\nevent containment, and teardown lifecycle. Static renderers keep the fallback."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cursor"},{"type":"text","value":" binds an application-owned controller in focus-snapped or free mode.\nIt is behavior, not a mark; add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"crosshair(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" when the cursor should have a\nrenderer-native visual guide. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./focus-and-interaction.md#controlled-cursors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus and Interaction"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tooltip placement policy stays with the definition. Add the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"portal"},{"type":"text","value":" extension\nwhen the surface must escape clipped chart ancestors. Framework-only content\ncomposition remains an adapter prop, slot, snippet, or template."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ResponsiveChartConfig<TSpec>"},{"type":"text","value":" combines those options with the responsive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chart"},{"type":"text","value":"\nbuilder. The two-argument "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineChart(definition, options)"},{"type":"text","value":" form creates a new\ndefinition when a reusable base needs a different interaction policy."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Definitions carry an optional fourth tooltip-host type parameter:\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartDefinition<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue, TTooltipHost>"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DomChartDefinition"},{"type":"text","value":"\nfixes that host to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"dom\""},{"type":"text","value":"; DOM adapter exports expose it as their local\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartDefinition"},{"type":"text","value":". Adding a DOM or React Native tooltip therefore makes that\ndefinition host-specific. A definition without a tooltip remains assignable to\neither host. Deliberately widening it to the generic three-parameter\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartDefinition"},{"type":"text","value":" erases that proof and is rejected by strict host props."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"identity-and-updates","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Identity and updates"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A definition captures application values. Its identity is the application\nupdate boundary: keep it stable until a captured value changes."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\nconst definition = useMemo(() => {\n  const ranked = rows\n    .map((row) => ({ label: row.label, value: row[metric] }))\n    .sort((left, right) => right.value - left.value)\n\n  return defineChart(({ width }) => ({\n    marks: [barX(ranked, { x: 'value', y: 'label' })],\n    scales: {\n      x: {\n        scale: scaleLinear,\n        nice: true,\n        axis: { ticks: { count: width < 480 ? 4 : 7 } },\n      },\n      y: {\n        scale: () => scaleBand().padding(0.1),\n      },\n    },\n  }))\n}, [rows, metric])","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Framework adapters use their native memoization primitive. Vanilla code\ncreates the next definition and passes it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"host.update"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"types","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Types"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface ChartBuildContext {\n  width: number\n  height: number\n  defaultTheme: ChartTheme\n}\n\ntype ChartDefinition<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue> =\n  | StaticChartDefinition<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  | ResponsiveChartDefinition<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isResponsiveChartDefinition"},{"type":"text","value":" narrows the union to a builder definition."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"definechart","text":"defineChart","level":2},{"id":"static-definitions","text":"Static definitions","level":2},{"id":"responsive-definitions","text":"Responsive definitions","level":2},{"id":"definition-behavior","text":"Definition behavior","level":2},{"id":"identity-and-updates","text":"Identity and updates","level":2},{"id":"types","text":"Types","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## `defineChart`\n\n```ts\nimport { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\nimport { portal } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip/portal'\n```\n\n`defineChart` accepts a complete chart spec, a responsive configuration, or an\nexisting definition plus replacement behavior:\n\n```ts\nfunction defineChart<const TMarks, const TSpec>(\n  spec: TSpec,\n): StaticChartDefinition<InferredDatum, InferredX, InferredY>\n\nfunction defineChart<const TSpec>(\n  chart: (context: ChartBuildContext) => TSpec,\n): ResponsiveChartDefinition<InferredDatum, InferredX, InferredY>\n\nfunction defineChart<const TSpec>(\n  config: ResponsiveChartConfig<TSpec>,\n): ResponsiveChartDefinition<InferredDatum, InferredX, InferredY>\n\nfunction defineChart<TDefinition, TOptions>(\n  definition: TDefinition,\n  options: TOptions,\n): Omit<TDefinition, keyof TOptions> & TOptions\n```\n\n## Static definitions\n\nUse a static definition when its data and visual options are already known:\n\n```ts\nimport { scaleUtc } from 'd3-scale'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks: [lineY(rows, { x: 'date', y: 'value' })],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: scaleUtc },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear, nice: true, grid: true },\n  },\n\n  focus: 'group-x',\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    portal,\n    anchor: 'group-center',\n    placement: ['top', 'right', 'left', 'bottom'],\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Responsive definitions\n\nUse a configuration object when the spec depends on the resolved chart\nsurface:\n\n```ts\nimport { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  svgAnimation: true,\n  chart: ({ width }) => ({\n    marks: [barY(rows, { x: 'category', y: 'value' })],\n    scales: {\n      x: { scale: scaleBand },\n      y: {\n        scale: scaleLinear,\n        nice: true,\n        axis: { ticks: { count: width < 480 ? 4 : 7 } },\n        grid: true,\n      },\n    },\n  }),\n})\n```\n\nThe builder receives:\n\n| Property       | Type         | Meaning                                                      |\n| -------------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `width`        | `number`     | Current full surface width                                   |\n| `height`       | `number`     | Current full surface height                                  |\n| `defaultTheme` | `ChartTheme` | Platform defaults before the returned spec applies its theme |\n\n`width` and `height` are controlled by the host. The builder can read them but\ndoes not return or own them.\n\n## Definition behavior\n\n`ChartDefinitionOptions<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>` contains `focus`,\n`focusRing`, `selection`, `controls`, `cursor`, `maxFocusDistance`,\n`spatialIndex`, `svgAnimation`, `pointer`, `keyboard`, and `tooltip`. These options\nbelong to both static and responsive definitions. Hosts and framework adapters\ndo not override them.\n\n`focusRing` accepts `true`, `false`, or a `ChartFocusRingOptions` object with\n`radius`, `strokeWidth`, `fill`, and `stroke`. Omitted fields keep the built-in\ndefaults, including the focused point's resolved color for `stroke`. The same\nvalue on `theme.focusRing` provides a default, while an explicitly supplied\ndefinition-level value takes precedence. See\n[Focus and interaction](./focus-and-interaction.md#built-in-focus-ring).\n\nEach `ChartControl` resolves after final scales and plot bounds exist. It can\nprovide renderer-neutral fallback nodes and an optional host control. Control\nIDs and host-control identities must be unique. Browser hosts remove a\ncontrol's fallback before painting and own its update, renderer replacement,\nevent containment, and teardown lifecycle. Static renderers keep the fallback.\n\n`cursor` binds an application-owned controller in focus-snapped or free mode.\nIt is behavior, not a mark; add `crosshair(...)` when the cursor should have a\nrenderer-native visual guide. See\n[Focus and Interaction](./focus-and-interaction.md#controlled-cursors).\n\nTooltip placement policy stays with the definition. Add the `portal` extension\nwhen the surface must escape clipped chart ancestors. Framework-only content\ncomposition remains an adapter prop, slot, snippet, or template.\n\n`ResponsiveChartConfig<TSpec>` combines those options with the responsive `chart`\nbuilder. The two-argument `defineChart(definition, options)` form creates a new\ndefinition when a reusable base needs a different interaction policy.\n\nDefinitions carry an optional fourth tooltip-host type parameter:\n`ChartDefinition<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue, TTooltipHost>`. `DomChartDefinition`\nfixes that host to `\"dom\"`; DOM adapter exports expose it as their local\n`ChartDefinition`. Adding a DOM or React Native tooltip therefore makes that\ndefinition host-specific. A definition without a tooltip remains assignable to\neither host. Deliberately widening it to the generic three-parameter\n`ChartDefinition` erases that proof and is rejected by strict host props.\n\n## Identity and updates\n\nA definition captures application values. Its identity is the application\nupdate boundary: keep it stable until a captured value changes.\n\n```tsx\nimport { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\nconst definition = useMemo(() => {\n  const ranked = rows\n    .map((row) => ({ label: row.label, value: row[metric] }))\n    .sort((left, right) => right.value - left.value)\n\n  return defineChart(({ width }) => ({\n    marks: [barX(ranked, { x: 'value', y: 'label' })],\n    scales: {\n      x: {\n        scale: scaleLinear,\n        nice: true,\n        axis: { ticks: { count: width < 480 ? 4 : 7 } },\n      },\n      y: {\n        scale: () => scaleBand().padding(0.1),\n      },\n    },\n  }))\n}, [rows, metric])\n```\n\nFramework adapters use their native memoization primitive. Vanilla code\ncreates the next definition and passes it to `host.update`.\n\n## Types\n\n```ts\ninterface ChartBuildContext {\n  width: number\n  height: number\n  defaultTheme: ChartTheme\n}\n\ntype ChartDefinition<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue> =\n  | StaticChartDefinition<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  | ResponsiveChartDefinition<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n```\n\n`isResponsiveChartDefinition` narrows the union to a builder definition.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Chart Definition API\ndescription: Reference static and responsive chart definitions, build context, and identity-based updates.\n---\n\n## `defineChart`\n\n```ts\nimport { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\nimport { portal } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip/portal'\n```\n\n`defineChart` accepts a complete chart spec, a responsive configuration, or an\nexisting definition plus replacement behavior:\n\n```ts\nfunction defineChart<const TMarks, const TSpec>(\n  spec: TSpec,\n): StaticChartDefinition<InferredDatum, InferredX, InferredY>\n\nfunction defineChart<const TSpec>(\n  chart: (context: ChartBuildContext) => TSpec,\n): ResponsiveChartDefinition<InferredDatum, InferredX, InferredY>\n\nfunction defineChart<const TSpec>(\n  config: ResponsiveChartConfig<TSpec>,\n): ResponsiveChartDefinition<InferredDatum, InferredX, InferredY>\n\nfunction defineChart<TDefinition, TOptions>(\n  definition: TDefinition,\n  options: TOptions,\n): Omit<TDefinition, keyof TOptions> & TOptions\n```\n\n## Static definitions\n\nUse a static definition when its data and visual options are already known:\n\n```ts\nimport { scaleUtc } from 'd3-scale'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  marks: [lineY(rows, { x: 'date', y: 'value' })],\n  scales: {\n    x: { scale: scaleUtc },\n    y: { scale: scaleLinear, nice: true, grid: true },\n  },\n\n  focus: 'group-x',\n  tooltip: {\n    use: tooltip,\n    portal,\n    anchor: 'group-center',\n    placement: ['top', 'right', 'left', 'bottom'],\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Responsive definitions\n\nUse a configuration object when the spec depends on the resolved chart\nsurface:\n\n```ts\nimport { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\nconst definition = defineChart({\n  svgAnimation: true,\n  chart: ({ width }) => ({\n    marks: [barY(rows, { x: 'category', y: 'value' })],\n    scales: {\n      x: { scale: scaleBand },\n      y: {\n        scale: scaleLinear,\n        nice: true,\n        axis: { ticks: { count: width < 480 ? 4 : 7 } },\n        grid: true,\n      },\n    },\n  }),\n})\n```\n\nThe builder receives:\n\n| Property       | Type         | Meaning                                                      |\n| -------------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `width`        | `number`     | Current full surface width                                   |\n| `height`       | `number`     | Current full surface height                                  |\n| `defaultTheme` | `ChartTheme` | Platform defaults before the returned spec applies its theme |\n\n`width` and `height` are controlled by the host. The builder can read them but\ndoes not return or own them.\n\n## Definition behavior\n\n`ChartDefinitionOptions<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>` contains `focus`,\n`focusRing`, `selection`, `controls`, `cursor`, `maxFocusDistance`,\n`spatialIndex`, `svgAnimation`, `pointer`, `keyboard`, and `tooltip`. These options\nbelong to both static and responsive definitions. Hosts and framework adapters\ndo not override them.\n\n`focusRing` accepts `true`, `false`, or a `ChartFocusRingOptions` object with\n`radius`, `strokeWidth`, `fill`, and `stroke`. Omitted fields keep the built-in\ndefaults, including the focused point's resolved color for `stroke`. The same\nvalue on `theme.focusRing` provides a default, while an explicitly supplied\ndefinition-level value takes precedence. See\n[Focus and interaction](./focus-and-interaction.md#built-in-focus-ring).\n\nEach `ChartControl` resolves after final scales and plot bounds exist. It can\nprovide renderer-neutral fallback nodes and an optional host control. Control\nIDs and host-control identities must be unique. Browser hosts remove a\ncontrol's fallback before painting and own its update, renderer replacement,\nevent containment, and teardown lifecycle. Static renderers keep the fallback.\n\n`cursor` binds an application-owned controller in focus-snapped or free mode.\nIt is behavior, not a mark; add `crosshair(...)` when the cursor should have a\nrenderer-native visual guide. See\n[Focus and Interaction](./focus-and-interaction.md#controlled-cursors).\n\nTooltip placement policy stays with the definition. Add the `portal` extension\nwhen the surface must escape clipped chart ancestors. Framework-only content\ncomposition remains an adapter prop, slot, snippet, or template.\n\n`ResponsiveChartConfig<TSpec>` combines those options with the responsive `chart`\nbuilder. The two-argument `defineChart(definition, options)` form creates a new\ndefinition when a reusable base needs a different interaction policy.\n\nDefinitions carry an optional fourth tooltip-host type parameter:\n`ChartDefinition<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue, TTooltipHost>`. `DomChartDefinition`\nfixes that host to `\"dom\"`; DOM adapter exports expose it as their local\n`ChartDefinition`. Adding a DOM or React Native tooltip therefore makes that\ndefinition host-specific. A definition without a tooltip remains assignable to\neither host. Deliberately widening it to the generic three-parameter\n`ChartDefinition` erases that proof and is rejected by strict host props.\n\n## Identity and updates\n\nA definition captures application values. Its identity is the application\nupdate boundary: keep it stable until a captured value changes.\n\n```tsx\nimport { scaleBand } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/band'\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\n\nconst definition = useMemo(() => {\n  const ranked = rows\n    .map((row) => ({ label: row.label, value: row[metric] }))\n    .sort((left, right) => right.value - left.value)\n\n  return defineChart(({ width }) => ({\n    marks: [barX(ranked, { x: 'value', y: 'label' })],\n    scales: {\n      x: {\n        scale: scaleLinear,\n        nice: true,\n        axis: { ticks: { count: width < 480 ? 4 : 7 } },\n      },\n      y: {\n        scale: () => scaleBand().padding(0.1),\n      },\n    },\n  }))\n}, [rows, metric])\n```\n\nFramework adapters use their native memoization primitive. Vanilla code\ncreates the next definition and passes it to `host.update`.\n\n## Types\n\n```ts\ninterface ChartBuildContext {\n  width: number\n  height: number\n  defaultTheme: ChartTheme\n}\n\ntype ChartDefinition<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue> =\n  | StaticChartDefinition<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n  | ResponsiveChartDefinition<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>\n```\n\n`isResponsiveChartDefinition` narrows the union to a builder definition.\n"}
